# clang-tidy configuration, run by the check_clang_tidy component of all.sh.
#
# The reference version is clang-tidy 18 (the package on Ubuntu 24.04). Other
# versions may report different results.
#
# bugprone-macro-parentheses enforces macro hygiene (see #9483): every use of a
# macro argument, and the whole replacement list of a macro that expands to an
# expression, must be enclosed in parentheses.
#
# Where a macro legitimately cannot follow this rule (for example macro
# arguments that are names of declared objects, or negative integer constants
# for error codes), suppress the warning locally with a NOLINT comment, ideally
# with a short justification.
Checks: '-*,bugprone-macro-parentheses'
WarningsAsErrors: 'bugprone-macro-parentheses'
